<title>UK: Sainsbury seen benefiting from new focus.</title>
<headline>Sainsbury seen benefiting from new focus.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>British supermarket retailer J. Sainsbury Plc could benefit from focusing on rebuilding the superiority of its offer as the environment for the sector as a whole improves, Miriam Shea of Goldman Sachs said.</p>
<p>&quot;The environment is improving, capacity growth is in line with demand growth,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>Goldman Sachs raised Sainsbury to &quot;market outperformer&quot; from &quot;market performer.&quot;</p>
<p>Shea said Sainsbury's focus on its offer meant that &quot;they are unlikely to do anything destabilising on price&quot;.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44171 542 7717</p>
